gametitle=Way of the Samurai 2 (NTSC-U) SLUS-20893 158FA006 (Undub)

[60 FPS]
author=heavyjam
description=Presents a frame every field instead of every second one, taking the game from 30 to 60 fps, and keeps it running at its normal speed. Way of the Samurai 2 steps its world once per presented frame with nothing measuring real time, so unlocking the frame rate on its own runs everything at double speed. The rest of the patch corrects that: the engine's frames-per-second constant goes from 30 to 60, which keeps every frame-counted timer (dialogue, events, the story clock) at the same wall-clock length; every animation clock advances half a frame per step instead of a whole one, which keeps walking, running, combat and NPCs at their original pace because characters move with their animations; and the jump physics (launch speed, air drag, gravity and in-air steering) are re-fitted for the half-length step, so a jump reaches the same height and distance in the same time. A 3-second walk covers the same ground at 60 fps as at 30. The evade hops, one colour fade, the water scroll and the per-step rates of the smoke, dust and leaf particles are halved to match. Camera easing is not corrected and settles twice as fast, and particles still expire on a frame count, so they die young. Costs twice the drawing per second. Applied at boot, so restart the game after ticking it.
